    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 139,
        "text": "Hi, Dr. Chen. Thanks for meeting me. I'm Mia, the exchange student from the business faculty. I'm here for the week 36 academic check.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "c5200decf359b1e2e37095d20ef69f6f6f42c782c62e125f65aec1c4c56c0b45",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 150,
        "sourceEnd": 276,
        "text": "Of course, Mia. Come in. So, you're doing the joint project with the engineering students, right? The one on campus recycling?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "126e1bbff3b7982e1fa05df6aba733b67ffbf32fe047555cd03cf3c0bc488eab",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 282,
        "sourceEnd": 390,
        "text": "Yes, that's right. But I'm a bit worried. My part is the survey report, and I have to submit it next Friday.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "70dd2b1413f3d967a7c459ae29c869624dd78894461731cc604b55ffca234bc6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 401,
        "sourceEnd": 445,
        "text": "Next Friday, the 15th. Okay. How's it going?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "9c198fbb5685ded24ad199679d2c717ad0786995e7849186ae57824923b623e6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 451,
        "sourceEnd": 629,
        "text": "Well, the data collection is finished. We interviewed 120 students. But when I started writing, I found some problems with my grammar. My tutor said my tense use is inconsistent.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "edb2f029ca0bc815de78e46ecdf9cb2a50ad7d7a6dff17754557537e710cae23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 640,
        "sourceEnd": 840,
        "text": "That's common in reports. You need to use the past tense for what you did, and the present tense for general facts. For example, 'We interviewed 120 students' but 'The campus produces a lot of waste.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "80fb064830df5561fc01810c9c6bd80fb530f6e0cc529176452603e60fdccd67",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 846,
        "sourceEnd": 950,
        "text": "Right. Also, I'm not sure about articles. Should I write 'the survey' or 'a survey' in the introduction?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "a8390015be78ef03fd539b77e88caa10293d670e960f63cf1f9ed8e3bab36671",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 961,
        "sourceEnd": 1123,
        "text": "In your introduction, first mention: 'a survey'. After that, 'the survey'. And check subject-verb agreement—like 'The number of participants was 120', not 'were'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "a0e8fde097d8b3ca3058bed9445d251e16ed3020200702744b8f47508dfa41d8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1129,
        "sourceEnd": 1232,
        "text": "Okay. And relative clauses? I have sentences like 'The students who they answered the questionnaire...'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "f17121588e33d9f7fbd8fafa4e07e43bf594decd00053505bfc75b3c307900e0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1243,
        "sourceEnd": 1332,
        "text": "That's a double subject. Say 'The students who answered the questionnaire...'. No 'they'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "0d477ff2fe89c46f0544548acef11ccd9ec8e8f40e8700bc229e456d44d5c85c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1338,
        "sourceEnd": 1451,
        "text": "Got it. Another thing: quantity expressions. I wrote 'a large amount of students', but my friend said it's wrong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "78e8fba76baf53f83d670fd2438a8478e0101d35e5a92c46bf9d752cb29a1f49",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1462,
        "sourceEnd": 1598,
        "text": "Yes, use 'a large number of students' because students are countable. 'Amount' is for uncountable nouns, like 'a large amount of waste'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "3c6abe0ef958ab9f0dd2dfa3481531bc99c7bc0a0bc10ddb1de4483e475b7477",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1604,
        "sourceEnd": 1685,
        "text": "Thank you. I also need to prepare for the transition check. What exactly is that?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "59ccd60d5f8932b3960211be1fd17a67564fc6688c8185bca766e08b161717a7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1696,
        "sourceEnd": 1887,
        "text": "It's a short interview where you explain your project and reflect on your learning. It's not a test of knowledge, but of communication. You'll present for five minutes, then answer questions.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "e0e382b1f9a32ff30d896736f730a0b0a2a29eddec39ec21a106b05ca66d7fd1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1893,
        "sourceEnd": 1928,
        "text": "Five minutes? I thought it was ten.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "08244e30eb4acf5bf4b4562ae5b4aedacc08c1463d651b8db87c6889f0109384",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 1939,
        "sourceEnd": 2035,
        "text": "No, five minutes for the presentation, then five minutes for questions. So ten minutes in total.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "a7ce9a3cf28d53ecabdd28e369199d27825e4d7cf0a104e3f2a0d2fbd25cd720",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2041,
        "sourceEnd": 2069,
        "text": "Okay. And who will be there?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "2915acb6d2463d3f204247eee734dc84a77f88ed85836530308f420e7786142f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2080,
        "sourceEnd": 2183,
        "text": "Two teachers, including me, and one student representative. The representative is from the second year.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "830e5539d7a0c884178aaa20b0419cfe1167f8290b8743b6dd4654da3fa69394",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2189,
        "sourceEnd": 2208,
        "text": "Will I get a grade?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "27179873c18452de9bc0c42c5bbe96b64dc79246f27120897e6d58f7d01c6ab0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2219,
        "sourceEnd": 2287,
        "text": "It's pass or fail, not a grade. But you'll receive written feedback.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "e7c3ffa102fe26b064a93e5c4f128a6258533012210786f921a348ddbd248017",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2293,
        "sourceEnd": 2403,
        "text": "That's a relief. One last thing: my friend said I should bring a printed copy of my report. Is that necessary?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "d5dcc92b2caf253e07bd2f90cb7c45071b1dc55c617d5f501dccab2fe2b599a6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2414,
        "sourceEnd": 2488,
        "text": "Not necessary, but helpful. You can bring notes, but don't read from them.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "cff5d869819074a489c9aa1aab3f79619f101cd70836fe6676253ca623383177",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2494,
        "sourceEnd": 2526,
        "text": "Understood. Thank you, Dr. Chen.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "9441dfe3064ed4333b6d688bcdac77ef7bbcac9f7e30c51e54a499ec7d01651c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "dr chen",
        "speaker": "Dr. Chen",
        "sourceStart": 2537,
        "sourceEnd": 2571,
        "text": "You're welcome. See you next week.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "82f95e15342fbdd86eb164db5ba9eb1e05fa195cb7e398f6c1fe0d90c07a95ac",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
